    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Biophysical effects of forests on climate",
    "problem": "Climate models inaccurately reproduce local climate effects of forests due to coarse spatial resolution and uncertainties, while field observations are insufficient for a global analysis due to their limited coverage.",
    "method": "This study uses a window searching strategy on global satellite data to compare land surface temperature, evapotranspiration, and albedo between adjacent forest and open land pixels, thereby quantifying the local biophysical effects of forests on temperature after controlling for background climate and elevation differences.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze the biophysical effects of forests on local climate using global satellite data, quantifying the latitudinal patterns of cooling and warming driven by evapotranspiration and albedo.",
